<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-diplomystus-dentatus-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Diplomystus dentatus detail-tier Turing wavelength (184.3 µm, 51.5 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 85.2/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 1. Schnakenberg reaction-diffusion on a no-flux flank, with D_u chosen so the Turing onset wavelength is 184.3 µm at 51.5 Ma. The rendered field's radial peak is 186.0 µm. Dispersion Pearson r is 1.000 (RMSE 0.00033) and the diffusivity sweep Pearson r is 0.997. Equal diffusion collapses a linear perturbation (std ratio 0.031). A 20 µm chromatophore is sub-wavelength and its lowest mode decays. The Descouens Fossil Lake photograph is the specimen; its major-axis spacing is an organ-scale contrast, not a fit to 184.3 µm. The growth GIF ends on that photograph (12 frames, 960×640). Overall 85.2/100 (faithfulness 84.6, reproducibility 86.8); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 78, Parameter expressivity 88, Morphometric validation 86, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 84, Reproducibility package 86. Output judged: docs/media/diplomystus_dentatus_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-diplomystus-dentatus-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d, image/png, 1059751 B, 1736×1176 px, artifact_sha256 337592b6425e02b45f9290c4e87ff91b95cc8f3998d8bfbacee70ff81612e229 (sha256 337592b6425e02b45f9290c4e87ff91b95cc8f3998d8bfbacee70ff81612e229), spec_fingerprint dca96e708aacc37802c4b54ab60381864ab6fced4c5a2aa1dbd4e8eeec3dd5e9. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: dca96e708aacc37802c4b54ab60381864ab6fced4c5a2aa1dbd4e8eeec3dd5e9; artifact_sha256: 337592b6425e02b45f9290c4e87ff91b95cc8f3998d8bfbacee70ff81612e229. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing (1952) onset wavenumber k_c^2 = (D_v f_u + D_u g_v) / (2 D_u D_v), lambda_c = 2 pi / k_c. | Schnakenberg (1979) kinetics du/dt = a - u + u^2 v, dv/dt = b - u^2 v. | Grande (1982) redescribes Diplomystus dentatus from the Fossil Butte Member: dorsal scutes usually 22-36, maximum length about 65 cm, ellimmichthyid rather than a clupeid. | Kondo & Asai (1995) and Nakamasu et al. (2009) show teleost skin can select a Turing pigment wavelength. | Smith, Carroll & Singer (2008) reconstruct the Eocene Green River lake system. Descouens' CC BY-SA 4.0 photograph is a Fossil Lake specimen with caption size 48 cm.; reconstructed_in_script: a=0.128, b=0.764, D_v/D_u=9.17, with D_u solved so the onset wavelength is 184.3 µm. Neumann explicit Euler on a flank window. These constants belong to slot 3170, not to the 7.56 mm sibling. | Discrete-Laplacian growth rates versus the analytic eigenvalue (Pearson r = 1.000, RMSE = 0.00033) and a diffusivity sweep of expressed wavelength (Pearson r = 0.997). | Equal-diffusion ablation (linearised std ratio 0.031) and a 20 µm predecessor mode with negative growth rate. | Segmentation of the Descouens photograph: aspect ratio, circularity, and a high-pass major-axis spacing used as an organ-scale contrast to 0.1843 mm.; transfer_boundary: Pigment kinetics are transferred from the teleost Turing literature onto a Diplomystus flank. The 184.3 µm value is the catalogued detail tier, not a melanophore count on the slab. | 51.5 Ma is the Ypresian chronoseries datum. The series contains one Diplomystus age (1/1); the predecessor and successor compared here are scales, not other chronospecies.; does_not_claim: That the fossil photograph resolves 184 µm ocelli, or that a, b, and D were measured in Diplomystus tissue. | That dorsal scute counts (22-36) are the same pattern as the detail-tier wave. | A new radiometric date for Fossil Lake.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'The flank field is an isotropic labyrinth. A dorsoventral anisotropy trial is still needed to see whether rib-aligned stripes can be selected without leaving the 184.3 µm onset wavelength.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'The 48 cm caption calibration of flank spacing has no uncertainty. Report a resampled interval.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Single builder-assessor. Do not invent a second provider score.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': 'The equal-diffusion ablation is linearised. Add a small-amplitude nonlinear control that stays inside the fixed-point basin.'}" ;
    pk:hasScore 8.52e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-diplomystus-dentatus-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Diplomystus dentatus detail-tier Turing wavelength (184.3 µm, 51.5 Ma) — Parameter expressivity: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Scaling both diffusivities by s^2 moves the measured wavelength along the predicted line (sweep r=0.997) from about 130 µm to about 280 µm. Equal diffusion is the off-switch and does not produce a wavelength." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-diplomystus-dentatus-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-diplomystus-dentatus-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

